OpenSSL 4.1.0: a GREASE ECH payload has a random length instead of a real offer's

Kuicksilver's own code, the seventh patch carried under ADR-0019 (docs/adr/0019-openssl-4-and-ech.md), applied after
openssl-4.1.0-ech-psk-after-rejection.patch; pinned by its SHA-256 in gradle/openssl.toml as patch_7, applied by
tools/openssl/apply-patch.pl to the verified tarball, and dropped with the first OpenSSL release that fixes it (upstream
report drafted 2026-11-19, to be filed). Applies to OpenSSL master at df4c3359 on top of the patches before it (git apply; extensions_clnt.c is 99
lines further down there).

The bug: RFC 9849 section 6.2.1 has a GREASE client "Set the payload field to a randomly generated string of L+C bytes,
where C is the ciphertext expansion of the selected AEAD scheme and L is the size of the EncodedClientHelloInner the
client would compute when offering ECH, padded according to Section 6.1.3." ossl_ech_send_grease (ech_internal.c) picks
144, 176, 208 or 240 at random, so the length of a GREASE payload tells it from a real offer of the same ClientHello
(section 10.10.4: GREASE must not be distinguishable from a real offer).

The fix: ech_grease_clear_len computes L from the ClientHello written so far, as ossl_ech_encode_inner would encode the
inner one (no legacy_session_id, the extensions a real offer compresses as one ech_outer_extensions, the others as they
are, an inner encrypted_client_hello, and the pre_shared_key still to come, sized by ossl_ech_grease_psk_len), padded as
ossl_ech_calc_padding does with a maximum_name_length of 0; the payload is L plus the AEAD's expansion. The RFC 8701
GREASE extensions (SSL_OP_GREASE) are not counted.

diff --git a/ssl/ech/ech_internal.c b/ssl/ech/ech_internal.c
--- a/ssl/ech/ech_internal.c
+++ b/ssl/ech/ech_internal.c
@@ -276,9 +276,60 @@
 
 /* GREASEy constants */
 #define OSSL_ECH_MAX_GREASE_PUB 0x100 /* buffer size for 'enc' values */
-#define OSSL_ECH_MAX_GREASE_CT 0x200 /* max GREASEy ciphertext we'll emit */
+#define OSSL_ECH_MAX_GREASE_CT 0x800 /* max GREASEy ciphertext we'll emit */
 
 /*
+ * The EncodedClientHelloInner length a real ECH offer of this ClientHello would
+ * have, padded as in ossl_ech_calc_padding() for a maximum_name_length of 0
+ * (RFC 9849, section 6.2.1: "L is the size of the EncodedClientHelloInner the
+ * client would compute when offering ECH, padded according to Section
+ * 6.1.3"). It is computed from the ClientHello written so far, as
+ * ossl_ech_encode_inner() would make it: no legacy_session_id, the extensions
+ * a real offer compresses as one ech_outer_extensions, the others as they are,
+ * an inner encrypted_client_hello, and the pre_shared_key still to come. The
+ * RFC 8701 GREASE extensions (SSL_OP_GREASE) are not counted. 0 on error.
+ */
+static size_t ech_grease_clear_len(SSL_CONNECTION *s, WPACKET *pkt)
+{
+    size_t written = 0, len, k = 0;
+    PACKET ch, sid, suites, comp, ext;
+    unsigned int type;
+
+    if (!WPACKET_get_total_written(pkt, &written) || written < 4
+        || !PACKET_buf_init(&ch, WPACKET_get_curr(pkt) - written + 4,
+            written - 4)
+        || !PACKET_forward(&ch, 2 + SSL3_RANDOM_SIZE)
+        || !PACKET_get_length_prefixed_1(&ch, &sid)
+        || !PACKET_get_length_prefixed_2(&ch, &suites)
+        || !PACKET_get_length_prefixed_1(&ch, &comp)
+        || !PACKET_forward(&ch, 2)) /* the extensions' length, still open */
+        return 0;
+    len = 2 + SSL3_RANDOM_SIZE + 1 + 2 + PACKET_remaining(&suites)
+        + 1 + PACKET_remaining(&comp) + 2;
+    while (PACKET_remaining(&ch) > 0) {
+        if (!PACKET_get_net_2(&ch, &type)
+            || !PACKET_get_length_prefixed_2(&ch, &ext))
+            return 0;
+        if (ossl_ech_type_compressed(type))
+            k++;
+        else
+            len += 4 + PACKET_remaining(&ext);
+    }
+    if (k > 0)
+        len += 4 + 1 + 2 * k; /* ech_outer_extensions */
+    len += 4 + 1; /* the inner encrypted_client_hello */
+    len += ossl_ech_grease_psk_len(s);
+    /*
+     * as ossl_ech_calc_padding() with a maximum_name_length of 0: a multiple
+     * of 32 octets, at least 128
+     */
+    len += 31 - ((len - 1) % 32);
+    while (len < 128)
+        len += 32;
+    return len;
+}
+
